--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,25 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The site exposes its features to AI agents as [WebMCP](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/) browser tools.
+
+**Declarative tools** come from annotated forms (`toolname` / `tooldescription` / `toolparamdescription`):
+
+| Tool | Where | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `/search` | Searches articles by keyword and category |
+| `update_reading_list` | `/reading-list` | Adds an article to the reading list or removes it |
+| `toggle_article_bookmark` | Article pages | Saves or unsaves the open article |
+
+When an agent submits one of these forms, the page responds with structured JSON through `SubmitEvent.respondWith()` and then updates the UI.
+
+**Imperative tools** are registered with `navigator.modelContext.registerTool()` in `src/scripts/webmcp.ts`:
+
+- `list_articles` – lists or searches articles (`query`, `category`, `limit`)
+- `get_article` – full text, metadata, outline and reading time (defaults to the open article)
+- `open_article` – navigates to an article
+- `get_reading_list` / `set_reading_list_status` – reads or changes the reading list
+- `scroll_to_article_section` – article pages only; scrolls to a heading
